==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|continual|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈtɪnjuəli/|/kənˈtɪnjəli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-continually.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|con|tin|u|al|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[continual]] manner; [[non-stop]].
# In [[regular]] or [[repeated]] succession; very [[often]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2007|author=George W. Norton; E. A. Heinrichs; Gregory C. Luther|title=Globalizing Integrated Pest Management: A Participatory Research Process|page=87
|passage=Guatemalan snowpea production has '''continually''' been harmed by insect and disease infestations.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|in a continual manner}} {{l|en|ceaselessly}}, {{l|en|incessantly}}, {{l|en|nonstop}}; see also [[Thesaurus:continuously]]
* {{sense|in regular or repeated succession}} {{l|en|by degrees}}, {{l|en|little by little}}, {{l|en|momently}}; see also [[Thesaurus:gradually]] or [[Thesaurus:sequentially]]

